# One checkout on both hosts (§5, "Filesystem hygiene"). Without this, a Windows
# clone with core.autocrlf=true gets CRLF while the working tree that generated
# the checked-in artifacts has LF — and content hashes computed over source
# files then disagree between a fresh clone and the tree they were blessed in.
# The weekly fresh-clone gate found exactly that on its first run.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and not to be normalized under any setting.
*.png binary
*.spv binary
*.ggrp binary
